From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: The ASF (WMContainer) objects and the ASF media sink (9401)

mf.dll's WMContainer functions were spec stubs and Wine had no wmcontainer.h. As Microsoft
documents them ("WMContainer ASF Components" and the tutorials that write, read and copy ASF files):
MFCreateASFProfile (streams by number, mutual exclusions, prioritization), MFCreateASFContentInfo
(GenerateHeader writes the Header Object and the Data Object's header, so header + packets is a
file; GetHeaderSize/ParseHeader read one back; GeneratePresentationDescriptor with the MF_PD_ASF_*
attributes), MFCreateASFMultiplexer (fixed-size packets of several payloads; End fills in the counts
and durations), MFCreateASFSplitter (any length types, multiple and compressed payloads), the profile
<-> presentation descriptor converters, and the ASF file and streaming sinks (MFCreateASFMediaSink(Activate),
MFCreateASFStreamingMediaSink(Activate)): the sink is its own ContentInfo, its SetProfile makes a stream
sink per stream, AddStreamSink adds one; the header is written again at Finalize. Written from the
public ASF specification; interface layouts as in the Windows SDK header (checked against mingw-w64's).
