+/*
+ * Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9401): the WMContainer objects of mf.dll, as Microsoft documents them
+ * ("WMContainer ASF Components" and the tutorials that write, read and copy ASF files with them),
+ * written from the public Advanced Systems Format specification.
+ *
+ * - ContentInfo: GenerateHeader writes the Header Object (file properties, a stream properties object
+ *   per stream of the profile, the header extension with an extended stream properties object per
+ *   stream) followed by the Data Object's header, so a header followed by the multiplexer's packets is
+ *   a complete file (the documented "write the header, then append the data object" sequence).
+ *   GetHeaderSize/ParseHeader read a Header Object back into a profile; GeneratePresentationDescriptor
+ *   describes it with the MF_PD_ASF_* attributes (MF_PD_ASF_DATA_START_OFFSET: where packets start).
+ * - Multiplexer: fixed-size packets carrying as many payloads as fit (media objects split over packets
+ *   as needed); End() puts the packet count, durations and maximum object sizes into the ContentInfo.
+ * - Splitter: reads packets (any of the specification's length types, multiple and compressed
+ *   payloads) back into samples per selected stream.
+ */
